Sparkle Ed25519 (EdDSA) public key — Scribe update feed verification.

  kheW6+auc5kQ2CXIk16mVq8YQ1vlVZm5eIfnJZG9VO0=

Generated 2026-08-19 with Sparkle's `generate_keys`. The PUBLIC key is not
secret and is committed deliberately: Sparkle bakes it into the shipped app as
`SUPublicEDKey`, and every user's copy carries it in order to verify that an
update was signed by this key. The PRIVATE key lives only in the login Keychain
of the release machine (item "https://sparkle-project.org") and must never be
committed, exported into CI, or pasted anywhere.

Losing the private key is unrecoverable in the sense that matters: already-
installed copies will refuse any update signed by a new key, because they only
trust the public key baked into the build they are running. Recovery means
shipping a fresh signed build out-of-band and asking every user to install it
by hand. Back the Keychain item up before wiping this machine.

How it is used (SPEC §6; T9):

  - `scripts/release.sh` bakes it into Info.plist via SCRIBE_PUBLIC_ED_KEY,
    which feeds `SUPUBLIC_ED_KEY` in project.yml:

      export SCRIBE_PUBLIC_ED_KEY=kheW6+auc5kQ2CXIk16mVq8YQ1vlVZm5eIfnJZG9VO0=

  - `sign_update` (same Sparkle bin directory as `generate_keys`) signs each
    release archive with the private key; the resulting signature goes into
    the appcast entry.
  - Local and CI builds leave SUPUBLIC_ED_KEY empty, which disables update
    verification — fine, because those builds never auto-update.
